alues":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4-dev7 and current master [89001f9]\n- Not reproducible in v4.4-dev6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS 24.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI encountered a strange problem where some `LightOccluder2D create shadow while others don't. It seems to be somehow related to the polygon. If I change the shape of the polygon it switches between occluding and not occluding. Interestingly, this does not seem to be true for all occluders and I'm not sure when it is the case.\n\nAdditionally, I'm also getting a crash on some scenes with \n\n```\nERROR: FATAL: Index p_index = 16 is out of bounds (count = 16).\n   at: operator[] (./core/templates/local_vector.h:177)\n```\n\nwhen creating a new `LightOccluder2D`.\n\nMaybe somebody can have a look at the mrp and make more sense of it.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe mrp contains two scenes. `light1.tscn` and `light2.tsnc` have 2 `LightOccluder2D` where one is creating a shadow and the other is not. Try changing the shape of the polygons.  One always creates shadows while the other does only sometimes.\nAdding a new `LightOccluder2D` in `light1.tscn` crashes the editor. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18214889/mrp.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.git